<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Balance Druid</span></h2>In Phase 5, you can at last finish the Legendary Quest Line and earn your Legendary Cloak. For Balance Druid, our cloak of choice is <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102246/xing-ho-breath-of-yulon">
<img alt="Xing-Ho, Breath of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_dragoncaster_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Xing-Ho, Breath of Yu'lon</span></a>, which comes with a variety of powerful stats, as well as a strong proc effect that deals a respectable amount of damage, especially in AoE. <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146197/essence-of-yulon">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/monk_stance_wiseserpent.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Yu'lon</span></a> can also proc your trinkets, helping us to get early procs in the fight instead of waiting for them!<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Balance Druid Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Balance Druid should typically use two passive trinkets, and sometimes one on-use and one passive, but rarely ever two on-use. In the case of Phase 4 of Mists of Pandaria, we will default to our two standard passive trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<br/>There are no active trinkets of note worth mentioning for Balance Druid, as all of our strongest trinkets are Passive Trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105422/purified-bindings-of-immerseus">
<img alt="Purified Bindings of Immerseus" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Bindings of Immerseus</span></a> is by far our best option for a trinket in T16. Not only does it have a high intellect proc, but the amplification effect is very strong considering the amount of stats we possess in T16. There is no better trinket for the rest of the game.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105540/kardris-toxic-totem">
<img alt="Kardris' Toxic Totem" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_13.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Kardris' Toxic Totem</span></a>  also comes with a strong proc as well as a new unique effect, causing our attacks to sometimes perform "Multistrike". While this effect is only about 4% of our damage, it is enough to push it into second place as our trinket of choice.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105648/black-blood-of-yshaarj">
<img alt="Black Blood of Y'Shaarj" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Black Blood of Y'Shaarj</span></a> is another strong trinket, but lacks the bonus effect seen on our other two best options. It can also be somewhat difficult to fully optimize, as the ramping buff relies on us snapshotting DoTs towards the end of the spell.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105572/frenzied-crystal-of-rage">
<img alt="Frenzied Crystal of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Frenzied Crystal of Rage</span></a>  is our final option, and while it can perform well on stacked AoE, the low proc chance and lack of other strong effects make it slightly worse than the best two options.</div></li></ul>
